{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Roars. And growls.</b> A strange word, because the guttural letter expands, and the future comes on the pattern of יפעל, since the ע of the root was one of the gutturals. Only, if he meant to say thus, it is not possible for it to be altogether on the pattern of יפעול:" "<b>And he will spit out.</b> It appears that he spits out to see whether there is any rescuer."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra calls שאגה 'a strange word' and discusses why it deviates from expected morphological patterns; the argument is compressed and technically obscure but translated as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:26.944842430Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}